Problem description
- There is a finite set $$\mathcal{P}$$ of product types, indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$, and a finite set $$\mathcal{R}$$ of resource types, indexed by $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$.
- The planning horizon is represented by $$\mathcal{T}$$. This is a single-period production planning problem, so all decisions are made for one planning period.
- For each product type $$p$$, the input data include unit profit $$\pi_p$$, resource usage coefficients $$a_{r,p}$$ for each resource $$r$$, and a market demand upper bound $$d_p$$.
- For each resource type $$r$$, the available capacity is $$b_r$$.
- The planning goal is to choose production quantities that maximize total profit.
- Production for each product type must not exceed its market demand limit.
- Total consumption of each resource across all produced products must stay within the available capacity.
- Production quantities must be feasible for discrete units and cannot be negative.

- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_p$$: the production quantity of product type $$p$$.
  - $$Z$$: the total profit achieved by the production plan.

Input Format
{
  "planning_horizon": {
    "type": "single_period",
    "period_count": "$$H$$"
  },
  "products": {
    "count": "$$P$$",
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{P}$$",
    "unit_profit": "$$\\pi_p$$ for each $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$",
    "resource_requirements": {
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{R}| \\times |\\mathcal{P}|$$",
      "meaning": "$$a_{r,p}$$ is the amount of resource $$r$$ required to produce one unit of product $$p$$"
    },
    "demand_upper_bounds": "$$d_p$$ for each $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$"
  },
  "resources": {
    "count": "$$R$$",
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{R}$$",
    "capacities": "$$b_r$$ for each $$r \\in \\mathcal{R}$$"
  },
  "decision_variables": {
    "production_quantities": "$$x_p$$ for each $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "values": "$$x_p$$ for each $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$",
    "meaning": "the chosen production quantity of each product type"
  },
  "objective_value": {
    "symbol": "$$Z$$",
    "meaning": "the maximum total profit"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "planning_horizon": {
    "type": "single_period",
    "period_count": 1
  },
  "products": [
    {
      "name": "high_end",
      "unit_profit": 300,
      "labor_requirement": 17,
      "inspection_requirement": 8,
      "demand_upper_bound": 50
    },
    {
      "name": "mid_range",
      "unit_profit": 200,
      "labor_requirement": 10,
      "inspection_requirement": 4,
      "demand_upper_bound": 80
    },
    {
      "name": "low_end",
      "unit_profit": 100,
      "labor_requirement": 2,
      "inspection_requirement": 2,
      "demand_upper_bound": 150
    }
  ],
  "resources": {
    "labor_capacity": 1000,
    "inspection_capacity": 500
  }
}
